ROW: JOB QUEUE LATENCY (on-droplet, real worker claims real jobs)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Queue: pg-boss (schema `pgboss`, table `pgboss.job`). The app image bundles
pg-boss inside the traced server bundle (not requireable from the container),
so probes were enqueued by INSERTing rows shaped exactly like the queue's own
cron-produced rows (same defaults: retry_limit 5, retry_backoff, policy
'standard', dead_letter 'core.deadLetter', deletion_seconds 2592000), on a real
queue the running worker executes: core.reapAgentLeases (schedule * * * * *,
handler reapExpiredLeases — trivial, safe). Sequential probes on an otherwise
idle queue (the repo harness's baseline discipline); created_on -> started_on
read from the job row, the same clock the repo harness uses.

Method note learned in-flight: an earlier attempt ran while the browser/tunnel
measurements were hammering the single vCPU, and claims stalled ~7 minutes —
starvation under measurement load, not baseline. That pass was discarded (the
harness rule: baseline is an idle-queue measurement). Leftover probe rows were
verified completed, then the box was left to settle before this timed pass.

