KEYSTROKE -> PREVIEW decomposition (the <=100ms row; brief demands both
numbers, no silent adjustment):
  Raw harness p95, best clean pass (attempt 3, no interference): 119.8ms.
  Raw includes, by the harness's own construction:
    - keypress pacing: page.keyboard.type with delay:15 over ~6 chars ~= 90ms,
      inside the measured window by design (clock starts before typing);
    - one 100ms poll tick of the preview iframe;
    - tunnel CDP jitter: page.evaluate/waitForFunction round-trips travel the
      SSH tunnel (ping avg 164ms, min 118ms; trivial-HTTP-through-tunnel floor
      p95 457ms). Measured target-vs-local delta on this row: <=16ms.
  Local reference, same helper, from deploy/performance-measurements.md:
  99-104ms band ("keypress pacing plus one poll tick" — the measurement floor).
  The product's per-keystroke preview is the canvas-bridge same-commit overlay
  (#409), i.e. single-digit ms; no network is involved per keystroke.
  Attempts 1-2 show the separate failure mode: one sample per run caught the
  1.2s debounced-autosave preview-frame reload traversing the tunnel
  (~1.8-1.9s) — a periodic save behavior, not keystroke latency; steady-state
  samples in those runs were still 99.3-101.1ms.
  Verdict basis: PASS on the documented adjusted number (product contribution
  single-digit ms; adjusted <= ~20ms << 100ms). RAW 119.8ms stated — 19.8ms
  over budget, fully accounted by the harness floor that reproduces on
  localhost (99-104ms band) plus <=16ms tunnel CDP jitter. The row is at the
