ROW: MIGRATION, MEDIUM DATASET (full chain apply, on-droplet, scratch DB)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The full migration chain ships in the app image at /app/db/migrations
(19 files: 0000_reviewed-baseline.sql ... 0018_area_delivery_windows.sql +
drizzle meta). Method per the brief: scratch DB in the droplet's postgres,
each file applied with psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f, wall-clock timed on the
droplet. (The repo's local family times the same chain through drizzle's
migrateToLatest on a fresh disposable DB — this is the same largest-workload
measurement through the app's own SQL files; like the repo family it applies
over empty tables, so it proves the apply window, not data-backfill cost.)

Command shape (run on the droplet):
  createdb scratch_mig
  for f in /app/db/migrations/*.sql:            # list expanded INSIDE the app
    docker compose exec -T app cat $f | docker compose exec -T db \
      psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -U freeholder -h localhost -d scratch_mig -f -
  # wall clock from before the loop to after

